CM The 51-segment EX 4 dipole written as two collinear GW cards, current-source
CM fed at the join.
CM
CM Physically identical to dipole-ex4-freesp-51seg.nec, so it must solve to the
CM same impedance and must deliver the 1 A the EX card asks for.
CM
CM It did neither. `solve_hallen_current_source` pins I = 0 at the first and last
CM segment of every entry in the endpoint list, and the current-source path handed
CM it the raw per-GW list — so the join carried a spurious zero. With the source
CM sitting on it the solver was asked for I = 1 and I = 0 at the same segment and
CM least squares split the difference: 36.953 + j7.013 ohm at I = 0.5, exit 0, no
CM warning (FND-048).
CM
CM Neither existing EX 4 fixture is split, so nothing caught it.
CE
GW 1 26 0 0 -5.282 0 0 0 0.001
GW 2 25 0 0 0 0 0 5.282 0.001
GE 0
EX 4 1 26 0 1.0 0.0
FR 0 1 0 0 14.2 0
EN
